
    Suppose you want to have fptk as a local 3rd-party lib in your "proj" package.
    Suppose you want to have it placed at: proj/utils/fptk_local

    Then:
    1) You'll have to import fptk as:
       @@ import proj.utils.fptk_local.core
       @@ require proj.utils.fptk_local.core *
    2) Accordingly, in all fptk files:
       - all inner reimports must follow the same pattern:
         @@ require proj.utils.fptk_local.core.from_hyrule [->]
       - accordingly, macros one-shot-requirements must be:
         @@ hy.R.proj/utils/fptk_local/core/from_hyrule.->
         (yes, hy.R uses «/» for submodules)

    This is what fptk_local_gen (in scripts) does.
    fptk_local.loader is modified accordingly too.

    ------------------------------------------------
        
    When running simple script (non-package) «script.hy»,
    just place fptk_local in same folder, and importing via [³import fptk_local.core⁺] will work.

